        "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/_GlobalCrisis_/status/1958959983208403370",
        "text": "🇺🇸 Consequences of Hurricane \"Erin\" on the North Carolina Coast, USA \n\n🌊🌀 Hurricane Erin continues to have a destructive impact on the Outer Banks region of North Carolina.\n\n📍 During the evening high tide on Tuesday, August 19, water flooded the motel area in Buxton. Authorities warned that more serious consequences could occur during the following high tides — on Thursday, August 21, both in the morning and evening.\n\n📍 On Wednesday, August 20, during the evening high tide, water broke through the dunes near Avon Pier, flooding the coastal area.\n\n📍 That same evening, at the north end of Hatteras village, tidal waves from the storm washed over N.C. 12 highway, creating dangerous conditions for traffic. Eyewitnesses captured dramatic scenes of the ocean surging onto the road.\n\n⚠️ High waves and storm surge from Hurricane Erin continue to worsen along the Outer Banks, spanning from Corolla to Ocracoke, turning the coastline into a danger zone.\n🔗 Source: SamWalkerOBXNews\n\n 🆘 Rescue teams can’t do it all in a sudden emergency. That’s where YOU step in. 🌍 Connect, prepare, and help those around you. Together, we’re unstoppable. 💪\n\n👀 To learn more about the reasons of the increasing natural disasters and the way out of it, read the report ON THE PROGRESSION OF CLIMATIC DISASTERS ON EARTH AND THEIR CATASTROPHIC CONSEQUENCES\n🔴 https://t.co/17otvN87Jr\n\n#CreativeSociety #GlobalCrisis\n#Responsibility #ActNow #SPEAKUP\n#USA #NorthCarolina #OuterBanks #HurricaneErin #Storm  #ncwx #obx #NaturalDisasters #weather #climate #destruction #anomaly #climatechange",
